# Every secret in one place: ~/.secrets/secrets.env (mode 600, folder 700).
# install.sh seeds it from this template. THIS FILE IS COMMITTED; the filled-in
# copy never enters git.
#
# Edit it with `secrets`; scripts read one value with $(secret NAME). It is
# plain KEY=value and never sourced into a shell, so no process carries a token
# it does not need. Agents are kept out of ~/.secrets (bin/secrets-guard and the
# Claude deny rules). After editing, ~/wiki/vault-sync.sh copies it into the
# encrypted vault that iCloud backs up.
#
# Every line below is commented out: uncomment each one as you fill it in, so
# a placeholder can never pass for a value.

# Jira (ecfxdev). Token: https://id.atlassian.com/manage-profile/security/api-tokens
# Read by jira-api, start-day, end-day, sync-tickets, jt and mrglass, and by the
# team's ops skills through ~/.config/ecfx/jira.env, which links here.
# JIRA_HOST=ecfxdev.atlassian.net
# JIRA_USER=<your Atlassian email>
# JIRA_TOKEN=<api token>

# Slack MCP app for pi (its client id stays in ~/.zshrc.local).
# SLACK_MCP_CLIENT_SECRET=

# CodeCompanion's Claude Code adapter in nvim (`claude setup-token`).
# CODECOMPANION_CLAUDE_TOKEN=

# Proxy (sing-box VLESS), read by proxyctl. proxy/secrets.env.example says where
# each value comes from.
# VLESS_SERVER=
# VLESS_PORT=
# VLESS_UUID=
# VLESS_SNI=
# VLESS_PBK=
# VLESS_SID=

# nightbot local dry runs (the VPS keeps its own /srv/nightbot/.env, unprefixed).
# NIGHTBOT_GITLAB_TOKEN=
# NIGHTBOT_CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# NIGHTBOT_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# NIGHTBOT_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
